Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 09:46:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/44] feat: anamorphic lens - squeeze (hFOV + gate mask /
 squeezed frame), oval bokeh, horizontal tinted flare

Squeeze Factor widens the horizontal capture (hFOV from sensorWidth x S, vFOV through the viewport aspect) and masks the frame to the desqueezed format via the new r_LensLetterbox cvar; Show Squeezed Frame stretches the same band to fill the viewport instead (raw negative, negative cvar). Gather taps and splat quads scale x by 1/S for vertical-oval bokeh with energy conserved. The horizontal flare is a separate branch of the HDR streaks pass (own threshold, three-iteration horizontal march, coating tint via StreakParams2), independent of the blade streaks and strongest wide open. Fixes: anamorphic stretch ping-pong hazard; PostAA composite sharpening and lens optics now follow the remapped source coordinate (ghost image under TAA sharpening with squeeze / distortion). User-verified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017nykaDjTHxHDSo11CsYx6M
