--- /dev/null
+++ b/Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/AnamorphicSpec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,210 @@
+# Anamorphic Lens Spec
+
+Status: APPROVED FOR IMPLEMENTATION (2026-08-25). Author: main session.
+Scope: three physically distinct effects of an anamorphic lens, each on its own switch:
+1. **Squeeze** - wider horizontal capture for the same focal length, letterboxed to the
+   desqueezed format.
+2. **Oval bokeh** - out-of-focus discs are vertical ovals, height : width = squeeze : 1.
+3. **Horizontal flare** - the long tinted line thrown across the frame by bright sources off
+   the cylindrical front element.
+
+Everything below is a delta on the current tree. Build with the bundled CMake
+(`Tools\CMake\Win32\bin\cmake.exe --build solutions_cmake\win64 --target <T> --config Profile`),
+targets `CinematicCamera` and `CryRenderD3D11`, zero warnings. Do NOT deploy DLLs or shaders.
+All comments and docs in English.
+
+---
+
+## A. Component (`Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/Module/CinematicCameraComponent.h/.cpp`)
+
+### A1. New property group `SCineAnamorphicParams`
+
+Same pattern as `SCineStreaksParams` (memcmp `operator==`, `ReflectType` with a NEW GUID,
+label "Anamorphic"). Member `SCineAnamorphicParams m_anamorphic;` reflected as
+`desc.AddMember(&CCinematicCameraComponent::m_anamorphic, 'gana', "Anamorphic", "Anamorphic", "", SCineAnamorphicParams());`
+placed right after the `m_lens` ('glns') line so it sits under Lens in the inspector.
+
+| member | tag | label | type / range | default | description |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `squeeze` | 'sqz_' | Squeeze Factor | Range<1,2,1,2> | 1.0 | 1 = spherical. 1.33 / 1.5 / 1.8 / 2 = anamorphic: the horizontal capture widens by this factor for the same focal length, out-of-focus discs become vertical ovals of this ratio, and (with Letterbox on) the frame is masked to the desqueezed format. |
+| `flareAmount` | 'afla' | Horizontal Flare | Range<0,3,0,2> | 0.0 | Strength of the anamorphic streak: the long horizontal line thrown across the frame by bright sources off the cylindrical front element. 0 = off. Strongest wide open, fading out by f/11. Independent of the diffraction streaks. |
+| `flareLength` | 'afln' | Flare Length | Range<0,1,0,1> | 0.7 | How far the line reaches across the frame. |
+| `flareThreshold` | 'afth' | Flare Threshold | Range<0,50,0,20> | 3.0 | Scene HDR value a source must exceed to throw a flare. |
+| `flareTint` | 'aftn' | Flare Tint | ColorF | (0.35, 0.62, 1.0, 1) | Colour of the flare. Classic anamorphic coatings give the cyan-blue line; a neutral tint gives white. |
+
+`ColorF` is reflected by CrySchematyc (`CrySchematyc/MathTypes.h`); verify it compiles in
+`AddMember` - if it does not, fall back to three `Range<0,1,0,1>` floats `flareTintR/G/B`
+with tags 'aftr','aftg','aftb' and say so in the report.
+
+### A2. Field of view with squeeze (`ComputeVerticalFOV()`)
+
+The engine camera takes a VERTICAL fov and the viewport aspect. Current behaviour (keep it as
+the fallback): `vFOV = 2 atan(sensorHeight / 2f)`.
+
+```
+const float S = clamp(m_anamorphic.squeeze, 1, 2);
+const float w_mm = GetSensorWidth() * S;            // desqueezed horizontal capture
+const float h_mm = GetSensorHeight();
+const float formatAspect = w_mm / h_mm;
+const float viewportAspect = (float)gEnv->pRenderer->GetOverlayWidth() / max(gEnv->pRenderer->GetOverlayHeight(), 1);
+if (S > 1.001f && formatAspect > viewportAspect)
+{
+    // Fit the format's WIDTH into the viewport: horizontal fov from the widened capture,
+    // vertical fov derived through the viewport aspect (the bars take the rest).
+    const float hFOV = 2 atan(w_mm * 0.5 / f_mm);
+    return 2 atan(tan(hFOV * 0.5) / viewportAspect);
+}
+return 2 atan(h_mm * 0.5 / f_mm);                  // fit height (spherical, or format not wider than the viewport)
+```
+Decision (user, 2026-08-25): the projected (desqueezed) frame with bars is THE default and
+the only FOV rule; no crop mode. One presentation switch was kept on request: **Show Squeezed
+Frame** ('asqf', default off) pushes r_LensLetterbox = -formatAspect and the final composite
+stretches the same band vertically to fill the viewport (the raw anamorphic negative) instead
+of masking it. Identical frustum either way.
+`f_mm` is the breathing-adjusted focal length already computed in that function. If
+`GetOverlayWidth/Height` are not available on `IRenderer` in this engine version use
+`GetWidth()/GetHeight()`; verify.
+
+### A3. Letterbox push (`ApplyLensCharacter()`, editor-live like vignette/distortion)
+
+New renderer cvar `r_LensLetterbox` (section C4). Push
+`letterbox = (S > 1.001 && formatAspect > viewportAspect) ? formatAspect : 0`
+every time `ApplyLensCharacter` runs, with the same save/restore discipline as
+`r_LensDistortion` (`m_savedLetterbox`, latched with `m_bLensCharSaved`, restored in
+`RestoreLensCharacter`).
+
+### A4. Oval bokeh push (`ApplyDOF()`)
+
+Push new post param `Dof_User_AnamorphicSqueeze` = `S` (section C2). Add it to the save
+block and to `RestoreDOF()` (`m_savedDofAnamorphicSqueeze`).
+
+### A5. Flare push (`ApplyStreaks()` / `RestoreStreaks()`)
+
+The flare is independent of the diffraction streaks: restructure `ApplyStreaks` so the
+anamorphic params are pushed whenever `CanDriveRenderState()` holds, regardless of
+`m_streaks.bEnableStreaks` (that flag keeps gating ONLY the blade-streak params exactly as
+today - when it is off, the blade params are restored as today and the anamorphic ones are
+still pushed).
+
+```
+const float N = max(aperture, 0.7);
+const float wideOpenness = clamp((11 - N) / (11 - 2), 0, 1);   // 1 at f/2 and wider, 0 at f/11
+HDR_Streaks_AnamorphicAmount    = flareAmount * wideOpenness
+HDR_Streaks_AnamorphicLength    = flareLength
+HDR_Streaks_AnamorphicThreshold = flareThreshold
+HDR_Streaks_AnamorphicTint      = Vec4(tint.r, tint.g, tint.b, 0)   via gEnv->p3DEngine->SetPostEffectParamVec4
+```
+Save with `GetPostEffectParam` / `GetPostEffectParamVec4` under the existing
+`m_bStreakParamsSaved` latch (add `m_savedAnamorphicAmount/Length/Threshold`, `Vec4 m_savedAnamorphicTint`),
+restore in `RestoreStreaks`. `ClearSavedBaselines()` needs no change (it clears the latch).
+
+---
+
+## B. Renderer post-effect params (`Common/PostProcess/PostEffects.h/.cpp`)
+
+### B1. `CDepthOfField`
+- `AddParamFloatNoTransition("Dof_User_AnamorphicSqueeze", m_pUserAnamorphicSqueeze, 1.0f);`
+- `Reset()`: `ResetParam(1.0f)`.
+- `SDepthOfFieldParams::fAnamorphicSqueeze` (default 1), filled in `GetParams()` as
+  `clamp(m_pUserAnamorphicSqueeze->GetParam(), 1, 2)`.
+
+### B2. `CHDRStreaks`
+- Params: `HDR_Streaks_AnamorphicAmount` (float, 0), `HDR_Streaks_AnamorphicLength` (0.7),
+  `HDR_Streaks_AnamorphicThreshold` (3.0), `HDR_Streaks_AnamorphicTint` (Vec4, (0.35,0.62,1,0))
+  - for the Vec4 use the existing `CParamVec4` registration helper (grep `AddParamVec4` /
+  `RegisterParam<CParamVec4` in PostProcess.h; the colour grading effect is a precedent).
+- `SHDRStreaksParams`: `float fAnamorphicAmount, fAnamorphicLength, fAnamorphicThreshold; Vec4 vAnamorphicTint;`
+  filled in `GetParams()` (amount clamped 0..3, length 0..1, threshold >= 0).
+- `Reset()` resets all four.
+
+---
+
+## C. Renderer passes
+
+### C1. Oval bokeh - gather (`GraphicsPipeline/DepthOfField.cpp`, `Execute()`)
+
+After each of the two tap arrays is built (the 7x7 and the 3x3 loops), scale the horizontal
+component: `vTaps[i].x /= fSqueeze` with `const float fSqueeze = clamp(dofParams.fAnamorphicSqueeze, 1, 2)`
+resolved once near `fIrisExponent`. Vertical stays the spherical CoC; the oval is
+height : width = S : 1, matching the desqueezed anamorphic look. Both the polygon and the
+mask kernels go through this (it is applied to the finished tap, whichever path produced it).
+
+### C2. Oval bokeh - splat (`ExecuteSpriteBokeh` + `DepthOfField.cfx` VS)
+
+`vAspectRatio.z` is currently unused (the comment says so). Set `vAspectRatio.z = 1 / fSqueeze`
+and update that comment to "z = horizontal splat scale, 1 / anamorphic squeeze".
+
+- `DofBokehRefVS`: right after `OUT.QuadPos.xy *= vAspectRatio.xy;` add
+  `OUT.QuadPos.x *= vAspectRatio.z;` (comment: the pupil image is squeezed horizontally, so
+  the quad - and the mask sampled through it - is too). Leave `QuadPos.w` (CoC in pixels)
+  alone.
+- `DofBokehRefPS`: the oval covers `CoC^2 * z` pixels instead of `CoC^2`, so the
+  energy-conserving deposit becomes
+  `const half fSplatNorm = vDofBokehHighlight.z / (fCocPixels * fCocPixels * vAspectRatio.z);`
+  with a comment. `vAspectRatio` is already bound to the pixel stage (~line 785).
+
+When S = 1, z = 1 and both lines are identities.
+
+### C3. Horizontal flare (`GraphicsPipeline/Bloom.h/.cpp`, `HDRPostProcess.cfx`)
+
+`Bloom.h`: add `static const int kAnamorphicIterations = 3;`,
+`CFullscreenPass m_passAnamorphicThreshold; CFullscreenPass m_passAnamorphicStretch[kAnamorphicIterations];`
+initialised in the constructor like the others.
+
+`ExecuteStreaks()` restructure (keep every existing line's behaviour for the blade streaks):
+```
+if (!CV_r_HDRStreaks) return;
+params = GetParams(); apply the r_HDRStreaks==2 diagnostic override as today;
+const bool bBlade = params.bActive && params.fAmount >= 0.001f && params.nDirectionCount >= 4;
+const bool bAnamorphic = params.fAnamorphicAmount >= 0.001f;
+if (!bBlade && !bAnamorphic) return;
+PROFILE_LABEL_SCOPE("HDR_STREAKS");
+shared: names, pStreakSource/pStreakPingPong, texel scales, bloom composite weight;
+if (bBlade)      { the existing threshold pass + direction loop, unchanged }
+if (bAnamorphic) {
+    PROFILE_LABEL_SCOPE("ANAMORPHIC_FLARE");
+    // Own threshold pass into pStreakSource (the blade pass, if it ran, has finished with it):
+    m_passAnamorphicThreshold - same setup as m_passStreakThreshold, StreakParams1 = (anamThreshold, max(anamThreshold*0.25, 0.01), 0, 0)
+    // Horizontal march, three widening iterations (8^3 tap distances = the whole frame width):
+    dir = (1, 0); fStride = 1.0 + 3.0 * len; fDecay = 0.60 + 0.38 * clamp(len,0,1);
+    for it in 0..2: pass = m_passAnamorphicStretch[it]; same setup pattern as the blade loop
+        (last iteration: ONE/ONE blend into m_pTexHDRFinalBloom, source = it==0 ? pStreakSource : pStreakPingPong);
+        StreakParams0 = (fTexelScaleX, 0, fStride, last ? fAnamorphicAmount / fBloomCompositeWeight : 1)
+        StreakParams1 = (0, 0, fDecay, 0)
+        StreakParams2 = last ? (tint.rgb, 0) : (1,1,1,0)
+        stride *= 8; decay = decay^8
+}
+```
+For the blade loop also set `StreakParams2 = (1,1,1,0)` on every pass (the shader now
+multiplies by it).
+
+`HDRPostProcess.cfx`: declare `float4 StreakParams2;   // (tint rgb, unused)` next to the
+others, and in `HDRStreakStretchPS` return `cSum * (StreakParams0.w / max(fWeightSum, 0.0001f)) * StreakParams2.rgb;`.
+
+### C4. Letterbox (`Common/RendererCVars.h/.cpp`, `GraphicsPipeline/PostAA.cpp`, `PostAA.cfx`)
+
+- cvar `r_LensLetterbox` (`CV_r_LensLetterbox`, float, default 0, VF_NULL): "Aspect ratio
+  to letterbox the final frame to: black bars top and bottom when the frame is wider than
+  the viewport. 0 = off. Driven by the Cinematic Camera's anamorphic squeeze; can be set by
+  hand for a plain 2.39:1 mask." Register next to `r_LensDistortion`.
+- `PostAA.cpp` (~line 490): `distortionParams.z = max(CV_r_LensLetterbox, 0)` (x = k1,
+  y = viewport aspect already there).
+- `PostAA.cfx` composition PS (the one that calls `LensDistortUV`, ~line 948): after the
+  colour is fetched, `if (vLensDistortionParams.z > 0.01) { const float fVisible = vLensDistortionParams.y / vLensDistortionParams.z; if (abs(IN.baseTC.y - 0.5) > 0.5 * fVisible) OUT.Color = 0; }`
+  Update the `vLensDistortionParams` comment: z = letterbox aspect (0 = off). Bars are
+  hard-edged (a real gate mask is).
+
+---
+
+## D. Docs (English)
+
+- `README.md`: new "Anamorphic" section (the three effects, the FOV/letterbox rule, the
+  oval ratio, the flare's f-number curve) + the property table for the group.
+- `docs/ConsoleReference.md`: `r_LensLetterbox`; post params `Dof_User_AnamorphicSqueeze`,
+  `HDR_Streaks_Anamorphic*` in the params list.
+
+## E. Report back
+
+Per section: files/lines changed; anything you had to deviate on (ColorF, IRenderer size
+accessor, AddParamVec4 helper name); build output for both targets (must be 0 errors 0
+warnings). Do not deploy.
